#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""filter-shadowed-allow — drop ALLOW (r+w) entries that are strict ancestor
directories of a READ carve-out entry (read carve-outs must win; probed on
nono 0.79.0 that a read grant does NOT subtract write from a covering ancestor
allow, while deny would also kill the reads).

Comparison is realpath-aware: `~/.pi` is a host symlink into `~/.config/pi`, so
its grant silently shadowed the pi hook carve-out. Entries that are not
absolute-ish (`~/...` or `/...`) — relative `.`, rootless `**/` globs — are
never dropped. Glob segments never match literal segments, so
`profiles/*/extensions/hook` does not drop `profiles/core` (keeps pi's legit
profile writes). The pi hook write-denial rides the profile's top-level
`unsafe_macos_seatbelt_rules` (a write-only deny inside the writable dir;
macOS; Linux ceiling documented), so this filter is a no-op for pi; it remains
for read-only hooks with no dir write (omp).

Input: argv[1] JSON {"allow": [...], "read": [...]}
Output: JSON array of surviving allow entries, original order.
"""
import json
import os
import sys


